        "original_id": "18c3a55d-5aa7-5ae8-961a-05a2d465968a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Buick T-Type, Buick GS\n- Companies: Buick\n- Concepts: marketing designations, logo series, product revival\n\nFacts:\n- Since 1965, Buick has used the Buick GS designation on several high-volume cars built by Buick.\n- During the 1980s, the T-Type was a series of Buick logos that was popular for Buick products.\n- The T-Type marketing approach in the 1980s revived a similar Buick approach used in the 1960s.\n- Buick later revived the similar marketing approach again in the 1990s.",
